PROPOSED TAGLINES — CHOOSE ONE 
The current tagline — Strategy for Leveraging Disruptive Change — was well-suited to the early 
positioning but no longer reflects the depth and authority of where Resilient Futures has arrived. The 
following options are calibrated for a senior Australian Board and Executive audience. 
Option A — Lead with the problem (recommended 
primary tagline) 
Strategy for a world that won't hold still. 
Why: Short, confident, and immediately resonant for a Board director or CEO. No buzzwords. Positions 
RF as a firm that speaks plainly and thinks clearly. Works as a standalone line above or below the logo on 
all surfaces. 
Option B — Lead with the outcome (strongest for 
Strategic Fitness entry) 
Building the strategic fitness to lead through what 
comes next. 
Why: Front-loads the most powerful concept in the current product suite. Strong for audiences who want 
to know what the outcome of engagement looks like. Recommended if Strategic Fitness Workshops are 
the primary conversion pathway on the site. 
Option C — Lead with capability transfer (most 
differentiated) 
Making your organisation the strategist. 
Why: Directly targets the unique value of SiA capability transfer over traditional consulting dependency. 
Bold and brief. Excellent as a secondary strapline beneath Option A, e.g. Strategy for a world that won't 
hold still — making your organisation the strategist. 
Option D — Lead with clarity (most emotionally 
resonant) 
Strategic clarity when the conditions are anything 
but. 
Why: Acknowledges the lived experience of leaders in complex Australian organisations — the 
ambiguity, competing pressures, the sense that the usual tools are not quite working. Warm and precise. 
Strong homepage hero subheading paired beneath Option A. 
Advisory recommendation: 
Use Option A as the primary brand tagline across all surfaces. Pair it with Option C as a strapline on the 
homepage hero. This combination signals both the problem RF addresses and what makes its approach 
genuinely distinctive. If the near-term commercial priority is Strategic Fitness Workshops, A/B test 
Option B as the homepage headline and measure conversion rate to booked conversations. 
