PAGE 6 — OUR WORK 
PAGE HEADLINE 
Strategy in action. Real organisations, 
real change, real outcomes. 
Over 25 years, Resilient Futures has worked with Australian Boards and 
leadership teams across a wide range of sectors and contexts — from national 
peak bodies to health networks, higher education to manufacturing, and 
government. These are representative examples of that work and its outcomes. 
National Professional Association — Strategy for a Changing 
Profession 
SECTOR: Professional Association  |  SCOPE: Full SiA strategy engagement 
The Context: A national professional body representing tens of thousands of members was 
approaching a new strategy cycle against a backdrop of rapid change in the profession it represents 
— from AI adoption and changing workforce models to shifting government policy and evolving 
member expectations. Their Board and Executive recognised that the previous strategy cycle had 
produced good work, but that the planning approach itself needed to be reset for a more complex 
operating environment. 
The Engagement: Resilient Futures co-designed a full SiA engagement spanning Board and Executive 
workshops, structured stakeholder engagement, conditions analysis across global through to 
internal domains, and the development of a 2027–2030 strategy. The process built a genuine shared 
context for decision-making — not just a document — and produced clear strategic priorities aligned 
to the organisation's most significant opportunity-risks. 
The Outcomes: A Board-endorsed strategy grounded in an evidence-based understanding of the 
change landscape. Clear strategic priorities across a 2027–2030 horizon. A shared language and 
framework for ongoing strategic decision-making across the Board and Executive. A capability 
investment pathway aligned to future conditions rather than past practice. 
Primary Health Network — Strategic Fitness Under Structural 
Pressure 
SECTOR: Health & Human Services  |  SCOPE: SiA Facilitation + Conditions Analysis 
The Context: A regional Primary Health Network was operating in an environment shaped by 
simultaneous pressures: shifting federal funding frameworks, increasing community need, 
workforce shortages, and the complexity of coordinating services across a geographically diverse 
area. Leadership recognised that the organisation's strategy needed to be tested against these 
conditions, not just reviewed in isolation. 
The Engagement: A structured conditions analysis and strategic opportunity-risk assessment, 
delivered through Board and Executive workshops. The process surfaced the interdependencies 
between the forces shaping the operating environment and helped the leadership team develop a 
shared, prioritised view of where the organisation needed to direct its attention and resources. 
The Outcomes: A clear conditions picture with strategic implications understood at Board level. A 
prioritised set of strategic opportunity-risks providing direction for resource allocation. A 
strengthened governance framework for ongoing strategy review. Alignment between Board and 
Executive on what the next period demands. 
Specialist Medical College — Redefining Member Value in a 
Changing Profession 
SECTOR: Medical Education & Member Association  |  SCOPE: Full strategy engagement + value network analysis 
The Context: A specialist medical college responsible for training, education, and professional 
standards was facing both external and internal disruption. Changes to medical education, evolving 
models of specialist practice, and shifting expectations of what a medical college should provide 
were converging in ways that challenged the existing business and membership model. 
The Engagement: A comprehensive SiA facilitation engagement that combined conditions analysis, 
value network mapping, strategic opportunity-risk identification, and business model exploration. 
The work engaged Board, Executive, and key stakeholders in a structured process designed to build 
both strategic clarity and genuine alignment. 
The Outcomes: A redefined value proposition for current and future members. Clarity on new 
business and operating model directions. A strengthened relationship with key partners. A Board 
and Executive aligned on where to invest and where to evolve — grounded in evidence, not 
aspiration. 
Manufacturing Organisation — Strategy Reset Under 
Disruption 
SECTOR: Manufacturing  |  SCOPE: Conditions analysis, strategy stress-test, SiA facilitation 
The Context: A major manufacturing organisation was facing structural disruption to its supply 
chain, competitive landscape, and workforce model simultaneously. Leadership recognised that 
their existing strategy had been formulated in different conditions and needed to be tested — not 
just refreshed — against the current and emerging reality. 
The Engagement: A strategy stress-test combined with a SiA facilitation engagement. The process 
started with an objective conditions analysis — from global supply chain and energy dynamics to 
internal capability and organisational culture — and moved through to a structured reassessment of 
strategic focus and initiative prioritisation. 
The Outcomes: From Board to frontline, alignment on the real change landscape. A reset strategic 
focus anchored to current and emerging conditions. Supply chain opportunity and risk addressed as 
strategic priorities. A leadership team with a shared context and common language for ongoing 
strategic decision-making. 
